# SFNS-4 audit remediation

Validated 2026-09-13T17:50:21.600830+00:00. Resolves F1–F4 from `.conduct/audits/2026-09-13-358943e3-full-audit.md`; the audit is retained as a historical snapshot.

- F1: SecFn cache lifetime is bounded by role-binding expiry. Invalid expiry dates deny access. A fake-clock regression verifies denial exactly at expiry.
- F2: Public content-only memory updates omit absent metadata; the in-memory adapter preserves optional fields consistently with PostgreSQL. Tests verify preserved filtering and explicit replacement, including a real PostgreSQL public API journey.
- F3: Shared REST identifiers and Google Discovery path expansion reject standalone dot segments before HTTP dispatch. Tests assert zero dispatch and preservation of escaped valid identifiers in normalized URLs.
- F4: HttpError retains normalized response headers. A fetch-to-retry regression verifies a 120-second provider backoff using injected sleep, without waiting or making external requests. Unsafe-write retry policy is unchanged.

Validation: **508 tests passed** across SecFn server (13), MemoryFn including PostgreSQL (23), PlugFn core (227), and providers (245). MemoryFn/SecFn typechecks pass; package build gate passes. Both local Workers canaries pass. The disposable pgvector PostgreSQL 16 container was removed after testing.

The packed consumer gate rebuilt and validated **38 packages**, including packed Svelte SSR/hydration. Artifact set: `06b1960bd7fe1d32e9567f6edd4e9d1f51de418016982eb9ade0a88e35280274`; directory: `.conduct/SFNS-4/artifacts/06b1960bd7fe1d32`. Source hashes and action manifests were refreshed. Candidates remain unpublished; no commits or pushes were made.

User-owned live provider/Gemini testing remains deferred. Prior hosted Hyperdrive evidence refers to the earlier deployment; it was not rerun for these packages. Other audit observations, including complete per-action credential lifecycle coverage and resource hints, are separate from these four fixes and are not claimed resolved here.

