P2: Set-member environment enforcement is inconsistent with the single-secret path. When the caller omits `environment`, `resolveRuntimeSet` skips the scope-side environment check (raw `scope.environment` is undefined), while `readRuntimeSecret` defaults the environment to `development` — so the same token can read all environments' members through a set but only `development` through a single-secret read. And when an environment is supplied, the first member in a different environment throws, making mixed-environment sets unreadable to environment-bound tokens. Align the member check with the default used by `readRuntimeSecret` (e.g. `environment: scope.environment ?? DEFAULT_ENVIRONMENT`) or document the intended contract.

