<summary>High-Level Assessment</summary>

<dl>
<dd>

<br/>

>The following are alternative approaches to this PR:

<details>
<summary><b>1. Consume published runtime packages</b></summary>

<dl>
<dd>

- ➕ Reduces source maintained in this repository
- ➕ Creates clearer package ownership and upgrade boundaries
- ➖ Required candidate versions are not yet published
- ➖ Cannot atomically qualify contracts and runtime compatibility
- ➖ Introduces registry availability and version-skew risk

</dd>
</dl>

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>2. Split adoption by subsystem</b></summary>

<dl>
<dd>

- ➕ Produces smaller, easier-to-review pull requests
- ➕ Allows independent rollback of model, memory, secret, and integration changes
- ➖ Delays end-to-end Rex qualification
- ➖ Creates temporary incompatible package combinations
- ➖ Duplicates migration and packed-artifact validation effort

</dd>
</dl>

</details>

>**Recommendation:** Keep the coordinated source adoption for this upstream compatibility milestone because the candidate packages are unpublished and the execution, OAuth, memory, and secret contracts must be qualified together. Follow with independently versioned package releases so future upgrades can use published artifacts and smaller subsystem-focused changes.

</dd>
</dl>

</details>

