<details>
<summary>  3.  <s>Tokens escape their assigned environment</s> <code>✓ Resolved</code> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛨ Security</code></summary>

<br/>

> <details open>
><summary>Description</summary>
><br/>
>
><pre>
><b><i>verifyRuntimeToken</i></b> compares an environment restriction only when the request explicitly supplies
><b><i>scope.environment</i></b>, leaving an environment-bound token unchecked against an unresolved scope. When
>the environment is omitted, individual secret reads later default to <b><i>development</i></b>, while secret-set
>resolution removes environment from its lookup and decrypts members by identifier, allowing
>verification to reach secrets outside the token’s assigned environment.
></pre>
></details>

> <details>
><summary>Code</summary>
><br/>
>
><code>[secfn/server/src/vault.ts[R746-748]](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/179/files#diff-d9b90f14447c5925f609a065ceaab45ef2d92660649f31abbe12e934c1c427faR746-R748)</code>
>
>```diff
>+    if (token.tenantId && token.tenantId !== scope.tenantId) throw new SecFnForbiddenError("Runtime token tenant mismatch");
>+    if (token.namespace && token.namespace !== scope.namespace) throw new SecFnForbiddenError("Runtime token namespace mismatch");
>+    if (token.environment && scope.environment && token.environment !== scope.environment) throw new SecFnForbiddenError("Runtime token environment mismatch");
>```
></details>

> <details>
><summary>Evidence</summary>
><br/>
>
><pre>
>The route passes an undefined environment into verification, and the environment mismatch comparison
>is skipped when <b><i>scope.environment</i></b> is absent. Subsequent individual secret reads resolve the
>omitted environment to the default before lookup, while secret-set resolution excludes environment
>from its lookup and decrypts members by identifier, demonstrating that an environment-bound token
>can be verified before the effective secret scope is established.
