        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6ifG1H",
      "path": "secfn/server/src/__tests__/memory-adapter.ts",
      "comments": [
        {
          "body": "<!-- cubic:v=3dfdbefb-0f74-4372-96c8-f32768435f70 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=45d9ffc9-cc72-5ad7-bdfa-60c7157225c2 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP2: The reworked `transaction` now runs the callback against a snapshot and defers replaying every write (`snapshot.mutationLog`) to `this` until after the callback resolves, for **all** isolation levels — including `read_committed`. The previous `read_committed` path ran the callback directly against `this` via `callback(this as TransactionAdapter)` and wrote through immediately, so an in-progress transaction's writes were visible on the adapter before commit (rolled back on error). After this change, a `read_committed` transaction that writes and then reads back through the adapter no longer sees its own writes (the snapshot is stale), and a concurrent non-transactional reader of the adapter observes nothing until commit. Confirm no caller/test of this test adapter relies on the old read-committed write-through behavior, since it is a behavior regression for that isolation level, or keep write-through semantics for `read_committed` while using snapshot+replay only for `repeatable_read`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At secfn/server/src/__tests__/memory-adapter.ts, line 146:\n\n<comment>The reworked `transaction` now runs the callback against a snapshot and defers replaying every write (`snapshot.mutationLog`) to `this` until after the callback resolves, for **all** isolation levels — including `read_committed`. The previous `read_committed` path ran the callback directly against `this` via `callback(this as TransactionAdapter)` and wrote through immediately, so an in-progress transaction's writes were visible on the adapter before commit (rolled back on error). After this change, a `read_committed` transaction that writes and then reads back through the adapter no longer sees its own writes (the snapshot is stale), and a concurrent non-transactional reader of the adapter observes nothing until commit. Confirm no caller/test of this test adapter relies on the old read-committed write-through behavior, since it is a behavior regression for that isolation level, or keep write-through semantics for `read_committed` while using snapshot+replay only for `repeatable_read`.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -113,21 +119,39 @@ export class MemoryAdapter implements Adapter {\n+      const tablesBeforeCommit = new Map([...this.tables].map(([name, rows]) => [name, clone(rows)]));\n+      const versionsBeforeCommit = new Map(this.schemaVersions);\n+      try {\n+        for (const apply of snapshot.mutationLog) await apply(this);\n+      } catch (error) {\n+        this.tables.clear();\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>",
