wn writes (the snapshot is stale), and a concurrent non-transactional reader of the adapter observes nothing until commit. Confirm no caller/test of this test adapter relies on the old read-committed write-through behavior, since it is a behavior regression for that isolation level, or keep write-through semantics for `read_committed` while using snapshot+replay only for `repeatable_read`.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -113,21 +119,39 @@ export class MemoryAdapter implements Adapter {\n+      const tablesBeforeCommit = new Map([...this.tables].map(([name, rows]) => [name, clone(rows)]));\n+      const versionsBeforeCommit = new Map(this.schemaVersions);\n+      try {\n+        for (const apply of snapshot.mutationLog) await apply(this);\n+      } catch (error) {\n+        this.tables.clear();\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>",
